From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Will Faust <willtechnoduck@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 8 May 2026 23:58:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] iOS: refuse to compile guest RIP < 0x10000 to prevent cascade
 noise
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

After a NULL-vtable virtual call (`call qword ptr [rax+8]` with rax=0),
the guest's control flow lands at RIP=0x8. Without a guard, FEX
compiles a block at RIP=0x8, the block faults, FEX reconstructs an
exception, queues it on the guest stack, then immediately tries to
compile RIP=0x8 again — producing thousands of CompileBlock log
entries before SEH unwinds. Returning 0 from CompileBlock for RIPs
below 0x10000 raises C0000005 to the guest immediately so the first
AV is the only AV in the log.

Madeira-commit: 2c8a3fa32fd9a2f183e3b04069824f78269bbccb
Rebased: clean
Class: madeira-port
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-09-24-fex-latest-rebase.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/Core.cpp | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/Core.cpp b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/Core.cpp
index 8af9cfe..7dee404 100644
--- a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/Core.cpp
+++ b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/Core.cpp
@@ -892,6 +892,16 @@ uintptr_t ContextImpl::CompileBlock(FEXCore::Core::CpuStateFrame* Frame, uint64_
   FEXCORE_PROFILE_SCOPED("CompileBlock");
   FEXCORE_PROFILE_ACCUMULATION(Thread, AccumulatedJITTime);
 
+  /* iOS-Mythic: refuse to compile obviously-invalid guest RIPs. After a
+   * NULL-vtable virtual call (`call [rax+8]` with rax=0), control flow
+   * lands at RIP=0x8, which then loops compiling thousands of garbage
+   * blocks before SEH unwinds. Returning 0 here raises C0000005 to the
+   * guest immediately so the first AV is the only AV. */
+  if (GuestRIP < 0x10000) {
+    LogMan::Msg::IFmt("[iOS] CompileBlock: REFUSING low/invalid RIP={:#x}", GuestRIP);
+    return 0;
+  }
+
   LogMan::Msg::IFmt("[iOS] CompileBlock: RIP={:#x} MaxInst={}", GuestRIP, MaxInst);
 
   static_cast<ContextImpl*>(Thread->CTX)->SyscallHandler->PreCompile();
